powerpagecomponent.content:
{
  "source": "{% extends 'OT Layout' %}
{% block content %}
{% comment %}
  Remediation worklist (PP-12, PP-13).

  Working-day ageing against the BR-010 ten-day threshold, per OD-018 (resolved
  2026-08-30): Monday to Friday, the day a case enters remediation counts as day 1,
  and England's bank holidays are applied manually rather than encoded - so a period
  spanning Christmas or Easter reads older here than it truly is and a breach near a
  bank holiday wants a human look.

  The count runs in the browser rather than in Liquid because Liquid has no date
  arithmetic. It is fed calendar dates, not timestamps, which is what keeps it free of
  the timezone question app/src/lib/workingDays.ts has to solve: the server has already
  resolved which UK day each value falls on.

  A rejected sign-off (BR-008) resets the clock, and the period it ended is preserved
  rather than merged (OD-018). `al_clockstartedon` holds the start of the period now
  running and `createdon` keeps the original start, so an action that has been round
  twice shows both: the ten-day threshold measures the current period, and the earlier
  one is shown beside it rather than added to it. Merging them would report a case as
  breached on the adviser's second day of rework, for time that was never theirs.
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %}
  `integer` is the only safe coercion here. `times: 1` repeats a string rather than
  converting it, so page_number became a string collection and the comparison below
  threw. `default` cannot rescue that - it only substitutes null.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign page_size = 25 %}
{% assign page_number = request.params['page'] | integer | default: 1 %}
{% if page_number < 1 %}{% assign page_number = 1 %}{% endif %}

{% comment %}
  Two views on one page (project owner, 2026-09-10). Without `case` this lists the cases
  that have remediation on them; with it, that case's remediation form.

  One page rather than two because a second web page would need its own page template,
  component id and Restrict Read rule, and this site's deploys are exactly where that has
  gone wrong before (see Deploy-Portal.ps1). `case` is read the way OT Case Detail reads
  `id`, and it is only ever used as a fetch filter value, escaped.
{% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
  Case reference search on the list (project owner, 2026-09-10). Filtered in the query, not
  over the rendered rows: this list pages server-side, so a client-side filter would search
  only the page the user happens to be on.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign f_ref = request.params['ref'] | default: '' %}

{% assign case_param = request.params['case'] %}

{% if case_param == null or case_param == empty %}

  {% comment %}
    The list. Cases carrying at least one remediation action, one row each - an inner link
    to al_remediationaction with distinct, so the row count is cases and the paging is
    cases, not actions. Membership is "has an action", not a lifecycle status: an action
    that is finished still belongs to the case that had to do it, and a case whose status
    has moved on would otherwise drop out of the list with its history.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% fetchxml remcases %}
  <fetch count="{{ page_size }}" page="{{ page_number }}" returntotalrecordcount="true" distinct="true">
    <entity name="al_outcomecase">
      <attribute name="al_outcomecaseid" />
      <attribute name="al_casereference" />
      <attribute name="al_clientname" />
      <attribute name="al_advisername" />
      <attribute name="al_casestatus" />
      {% if f_ref != '' %}<filter type="and"><condition attribute="al_casereference" operator="like" value="%{{ f_ref | xml_escape }}%" /></filter>{% endif %}
      <order attribute="al_casereference" descending="false" />
      <link-entity name="al_remediationaction" from="al_outcomecaseid" to="al_outcomecaseid" link-type="inner" alias="rem" />
    </entity>
  </fetch>
  {% endfetchxml %}

  {% assign case_rows = remcases.results.entities %}

  {% comment %}
    The actions behind the cases on this page, in one read. Ordered by target date, so the
    first action a case matches below is its earliest - which is what the list shows, and
    what its age is measured from. Scoped to the page's cases with `in`, the same device
    the sign-off read below uses, so the scan each row does stays over a handful of rows.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% if case_rows.size > 0 %}
    {% fetchxml caseactions %}
    <fetch>
      <entity name="al_remediationaction">
        <attribute name="al_remediationactionid" />
        <attribute name="al_outcomecaseid" />
        <attribute name="al_actionstatus" />
        <attribute name="al_duedate" />
        <attribute name="al_completedon" />
        <attribute name="al_clockstartedon" />
        <attribute name="createdon" />
        <filter type="and">
          <condition attribute="al_outcomecaseid" operator="in">
            {% for c in case_rows %}<value>{{ c.al_outcomecaseid }}</value>{% endfor %}
          </condition>
        </filter>
        <order attribute="al_duedate" descending="false" />
      </entity>
    </fetch>
    {% endfetchxml %}
  {% endif %}

  <div class="ot-notice" role="status">
    <strong>Cases in remediation.</strong> Open a case to see what has to be put right and
    to record your response. Age counts working days, Monday to Friday, from the day the
    earliest action opened; bank holidays are not deducted, so an age spanning one reads a
    day high.
  </div>

  {% comment %}
    A GET form, so a search is a URL that can be bookmarked or sent to someone, and so the
    pager below keeps it.
  {% endcomment %}
  <form class="ot-filters" method="get" role="search" aria-label="Search remediation by case reference">
    <div class="ot-filters__grid">
      <div class="ot-field">
        <label for="f-ref">Case reference</label>
        <input type="search" id="f-ref" name="ref" value="{{ f_ref | escape }}" placeholder="Contains">
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ot-filters__actions">
      <button type="submit" class="ot-btn ot-btn--primary">Search</button>
      {% if f_ref != '' %}<a class="ot-btn" href="?">Clear</a>{% endif %}
    </div>
  </form>

  <section class="ot-card" aria-labelledby="ot-remediation-heading">
    <h2 class="ot-card__title" id="ot-remediation-heading">Remediation</h2>

    {% if f_ref != '' %}
      <p class="ot-filters__summary">
        Showing cases whose reference contains &ldquo;{{ f_ref | escape }}&rdquo;.
      </p>
    {% endif %}

    {% if case_rows.size > 0 %}
      <div class="ot-table-wrap">
        <table class="ot-table">
          <caption>
            Showing {{ case_rows.size }} of {{ remcases.results.total_record_count }} cases,
            page {{ page_number }}.
          </caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Case</th>
              <th scope="col">Client</th>
              <th scope="col">Adviser</th>
              <th scope="col">Outstanding</th>
              <th scope="col">Earliest target date</th>
              <th scope="col">Case status</th>
              <th scope="col">Age</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {% for c in case_rows %}
              {% assign c_total = 0 %}
              {% assign c_open = 0 %}
              {% assign c_first = null %}
              {% for a in caseactions.results.entities %}
                {% if a.al_outcomecaseid.id == c.al_outcomecaseid %}
                  {% assign c_total = c_total | plus: 1 %}
                  {% if a.al_actionstatus.value != 120910602 %}{% assign c_open = c_open | plus: 1 %}{% endif %}
                  {% if c_first == null %}{% assign c_first = a %}{% endif %}
                {% endif %}
              {% endfor %}
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">
                  <a href="?case={{ c.al_outcomecaseid }}">
                    {{ c.al_casereference | default: 'Untitled case' | escape }}
                  </a>
                </th>
                <td>{{ c.al_clientname | default: '—' | escape }}</td>
                <td>{{ c.al_advisername | default: '—' | escape }}</td>
                <td>
                  {% if c_open > 0 %}
                    {{ c_open }} of {{ c_total }} outstanding
                  {% else %}
                    All {{ c_total }} complete
                  {% endif %}
                </td>
                <td>{{ c_first.al_duedate | date: 'dd MMM yyyy' | default: '—' }}</td>
                <td>{% include 'OT Status Badge' status: c.al_casestatus.label %}</td>
                <td>
                  {% assign clock_start = c_first.al_clockstartedon | default: c_first.createdon %}
                  <span class="ot-age"
                        data-ot-age
                        data-opened="{{ clock_start | date: 'yyyy-MM-dd' }}"
                        data-created="{{ c_first.createdon | date: 'yyyy-MM-dd' }}"
                        data-completed="{% if c_open == 0 %}{{ c_first.al_completedon | date: 'yyyy-MM-dd' }}{% endif %}">—</span>
                </td>
              </tr>
            {% endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <nav aria-label="Pagination" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
        {% if page_number > 1 %}
          <a href="?{% if f_ref != '' %}ref={{ f_ref | url_escape }}&amp;{% endif %}page={{ page_number | minus: 1 }}">&laquo; Previous</a>
        {% endif %}
        {% if case_rows.size == page_size %}
          <a href="?{% if f_ref != '' %}ref={{ f_ref | url_escape }}&amp;{% endif %}page={{ page_number | plus: 1 }}" style="margin-left: 1rem;">Next &raquo;</a>
        {% endif %}
      </nav>
    {% else %}
      {% include 'OT Empty State' title: 'No remediation actions' message: 'A pass outcome requires no remediation. Cases appear here for any non-pass outcome.' %}
    {% endif %}
  </section>

{% else %}

  {% fetchxml remcase %}
  <fetch top="1">
    <entity name="al_outcomecase">
      <attribute name="al_outcomecaseid" />
      <attribute name="al_casereference" />
      <attribute name="al_clientname" />
      <attribute name="al_advisername" />
      <attribute name="al_casestatus" />
      {% comment %}
        The route, so the regraded-outcome cell below can say WHY it is empty on a case that
        will never carry a grade. Outer join: a case not yet routed has none, and an inner
        join would drop the whole case off its own remediation page.
      {% endcomment %}
      <link-entity name="al_reviewroute" from="al_reviewrouteid" to="al_reviewrouteid" link-type="outer" alias="rt">
        <attribute name="al_name" />
      </link-entity>
      <filter type="and">
        <condition attribute="al_outcomecaseid" operator="eq" value="{{ case_param | xml_escape }}" />
      </filter>
    </entity>
  </fetch>
  {% endfetchxml %}

  {% comment %}
    Read with a loop rather than `entities[0]`: an index past the end of an empty result is
    one of the shapes this Liquid raises "Index was outside the bounds of the array" for,
    and an unreadable or mistyped case id is exactly how that would be reached. The loop
    leaves `c` null instead, which the branch below already handles.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% assign c = null %}
  {% for row in remcase.results.entities %}{% if c == null %}{% assign c = row %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}

  {% comment %}
    Every action on this case, not a page of them: the form is the case's remediation in
    full, and a numbered row that continues onto a second page is not the form the project
    owner signed off.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% fetchxml actions %}
  <fetch>
    <entity name="al_remediationaction">
      <attribute name="al_remediationactionid" />
      <attribute name="al_name" />
      <attribute name="al_description" />
      <attribute name="al_actionstatus" />
      <attribute name="al_duedate" />
      <attribute name="al_completedon" />
      <attribute name="al_adviserresponse" />
      <attribute name="al_assignedcontactid" />
      <attribute name="al_clientcontactrequired" />
      <attribute name="al_recheckrequired" />
      <attribute name="al_changesadvice" />
      <attribute name="al_clockstartedon" />
      <attribute name="al_reviewinstanceid" />
      <attribute name="createdon" />
      <filter type="and">
        <condition attribute="al_outcomecaseid" operator="eq" value="{{ case_param | xml_escape }}" />
      </filter>
      <order attribute="al_duedate" descending="false" />
    </entity>
  </fetch>
  {% endfetchxml %}

  {% assign rows = actions.results.entities %}

  {% comment %}
    The Sign-off column (AD-095): the latest T&C decision per action, or the adviser's
    completion where none has been made yet. Each row does a nested loop over
    `signoffs.results.entities`, taking the first entity whose `al_remediationactionid`
    matches the row's action - an O(actions x signoffs) scan rather than a single indexed
    lookup. That is fine here: this is one case's actions, and each carries at most a
    handful of sign-offs.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% if rows.size > 0 %}
    {% fetchxml signoffs %}
    <fetch>
      <entity name="al_signoff">
        <attribute name="al_remediationactionid" />
        <attribute name="al_signoffdecision" />
        <attribute name="al_signedoffon" />
        <attribute name="al_signedbyname" />
        <filter type="and">
          <condition attribute="al_remediationactionid" operator="in">
            {% for a in rows %}<value>{{ a.al_remediationactionid }}</value>{% endfor %}
          </condition>
        </filter>
        <order attribute="al_signedoffon" descending="true" />
      </entity>
    </fetch>
    {% endfetchxml %}
  {% endif %}

  {% comment %}
    The regraded outcome the form's last block reports. Read for the case rather than for
    an action: a regrade is the case's, and a Tax-only remediated case (AD-055) has no
    outcome row at all, which is why the read below tolerates an empty result.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% fetchxml caseoutcomes %}
  <fetch top="1">
    <entity name="al_outcome">
      <attribute name="al_outcomeid" />
      <attribute name="al_initialoutcome" />
      <attribute name="al_finaloutcome" />
      <attribute name="al_finalisedon" />
      <attribute name="al_regradedon" />
      <attribute name="al_regradereason" />
      {% comment %}
        Carried into the regrade so a save against a stale read is refused rather than
        overwriting another correction, which is the same ExpectedRowVersion the Code App
        sends. Where it comes back empty the regrade simply runs without the check, exactly
        as al_RegradeCase behaves when the parameter is omitted.
      {% endcomment %}
      <attribute name="versionnumber" />
      <filter type="and">
        <condition attribute="al_outcomecaseid" operator="eq" value="{{ case_param | xml_escape }}" />
      </filter>
      <order attribute="createdon" descending="true" />
    </entity>
  </fetch>
  {% endfetchxml %}

  <p class="ot-back"><a href="?">&laquo; All cases in remediation</a></p>

  {% if c == null %}
    {% include 'OT Empty State' title: 'Case not available' message: 'This case does not exist, or you do not have permission to view it.' %}
  {% else %}
    <div class="ot-notice" role="status">
      <strong>Remediation for {{ c.al_casereference | default: 'this case' | escape }}.</strong>
      You can record a response on the actions assigned to you; the rest are read-only. Age
      counts working days, Monday to Friday, from the day the action opened; bank holidays
      are not deducted, so an age spanning one reads a day high.
    </div>

    {% comment %}
      The Tax check's notes (project owner, 2026-09-19). What the Tax checker wrote is
      context for putting the case right, and an adviser had no way to reach it: the
      remediation action carries the checker's fail observation through
      Remediation.Describe, but not the case notes, and the review pages are closed to them.

      Above the actions rather than beside them, because it describes the check as a whole
      and not any one thing the adviser owes.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% include 'OT Tax Notes' case_id: c.al_outcomecaseid %}

    <section class="ot-card" aria-labelledby="ot-remediation-heading">
      <h2 class="ot-card__title" id="ot-remediation-heading">
        {{ c.al_casereference | default: 'Case' | escape }}
        <span data-ot-case-status data-ot-case-id="{{ c.al_outcomecaseid }}">{% include 'OT Status Badge' status: c.al_casestatus.label %}</span>
      </h2>
      {% comment %}
        The outcome the remediation was raised for, read back out of the actions.

        It is not one of the numbered issues and is no longer raised as one: it is the result
        every issue in the table is a reason for, and numbering it among them read as one more
        thing the adviser had to put right (project owner, 2026-09-10). Remediation.Describe
        writes it in brackets at the end of the standing sentence - "...when the review was
        submitted (Tax check: Pass with issues)." - so it is already on every action and
        needs no column of its own.

        The marker has to be there before the brackets mean anything: an action raised with no
        reason behind it still carries the sentence, and a checker's observation is free text
        that may have brackets of its own. Once it is, the outcome is the last bracket the
        description opens, the observation being written above the sentence and never below it.

        Both splits are on one character, this Liquid having no multi-character split, and each
        is assigned before it is walked, a for tag taking a variable rather than a filtered
        expression. The two ends are taken by walking the pieces rather than with first / last
        or an index - the same caution the item split below is written with, on a site that has
        rejected both an index into a collection and a two-argument filter.

        Read across every action rather than off the first, so a case whose Tax and AQS reviews
        both raised remediation names both. The same block is in OT Case Detail.
      {% endcomment %}
      {% assign ot_outcome = '' %}
      {% for a in rows %}
        {% if a.al_description contains 'submitted (' %}
          {% assign ot_tail = '' %}
          {% assign ot_opens = a.al_description | split: '(' %}
          {% for piece in ot_opens %}{% assign ot_tail = piece %}{% endfor %}
          {% assign ot_reason = '' %}
          {% assign ot_taken = false %}
          {% assign ot_closes = ot_tail | split: ')' %}
          {% for piece in ot_closes %}{% unless ot_taken %}{% assign ot_reason = piece | strip %}{% assign ot_taken = true %}{% endunless %}{% endfor %}
          {% if ot_reason != '' %}
            {% unless ot_outcome contains ot_reason %}
              {% if ot_outcome == '' %}
                {% assign ot_outcome = ot_reason %}
              {% else %}
                {% assign ot_outcome = ot_outcome | append: '; ' | append: ot_reason %}
              {% endif %}
            {% endunless %}
          {% endif %}
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
      {% comment %}
        Drawn as the document, the same way the Checker Checklist is (project owner,
        2026-09-10: a remediation should read like the review forms). .ot-checklist is the
        V8 sheet - Calibri, every cell ruled, grey header bands - and is shared with the
        review page so the two forms read as one family.

        Nothing about who may write what changes here. The adviser's response panel is
        still rendered only for their own open action and the Contact-scoped table
        permission is still the boundary (AD-069); the supervisor's attestation is still
        gated on the create permission for al_signoff. Drawing the form does not add a
        write path to either.
      {% endcomment %}
      <div class="ot-checklist">
      <div class="doc-footer">Outcome Testing — Remediation and escalation | V8</div>
      <h1>Remediation and escalation</h1>

      <dl class="ot-dl">
        <div><dt>Client</dt><dd>{{ c.al_clientname | default: '—' | escape }}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Adviser</dt><dd>{{ c.al_advisername | default: '—' | escape }}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Outcome</dt><dd>{{ ot_outcome | default: '—' | escape }}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Case</dt><dd><a href="/case-details?id={{ c.al_outcomecaseid }}">Open the full case record</a></dd></div>
      </dl>

      {% if rows.size > 0 %}
        <div class="ot-table-wrap">
          <table>
            <caption class="ot-visually-hidden">Remediation and escalation</caption>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">No.</th>
                <th scope="col">Issue / fail reason</th>
                <th scope="col">Remedial action</th>
                <th scope="col">Owner</th>
                <th scope="col">Target date</th>
                <th scope="col">Status</th>
                <th scope="col">Age</th>
                <th scope="col">Sign-off</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {% assign row_no = 0 %}
              {% comment %}
                The form's last two blocks are read off the same pass that draws the rows,
                so they cannot disagree with them: `all_approved` is every action's latest
                decision being Approved, `form_source` is the first action carrying the
                adviser's three answers, and `latest_adviser` is the most recently completed
                action. They are rendered under the table, once for the case.
              {% endcomment %}
              {% assign all_approved = true %}
              {% assign any_rejected = false %}
              {% assign form_source = null %}
              {% assign latest_adviser = null %}
              {% comment %}
                The case's most recent supervisor decision. The sign-off read is ordered by
                al_signedoffon descending, so this is its first row - taken here rather than
                from inside the row loop, which would give whichever action came first in
                target-date order and not the latest decision.
              {% endcomment %}
              {% assign latest_supervisor = null %}
              {% if signoffs %}{% for s in signoffs.results.entities %}{% if latest_supervisor == null %}{% assign latest_supervisor = s %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
              {% comment %}
                A review raises one action per thing the checker marked down (2026-09-10),
                and every one carries the same provenance in its own description. Each
                record keeps it so it stands alone in Dataverse; the table shows it once
                per run of actions that share it, rather than under every row.
              {% endcomment %}
              {% assign ot_shown_note = '' %}

              {% comment %}
                Which checks are done with, so their rows can come off the form (project
                owner, 2026-09-10).

                A Tax-then-AQS case remediates twice, and the two are separate remediations:
                its Tax check raised five actions here and its AQS check eighteen. A check
                whose every action has been approved is settled, and its rows are drawn like
                any other with the approval named in the check's heading.

                Settled rows were collapsed away between 2026-09-10 and 2026-09-11 (AD-114c).
                That is reversed: the T&C Supervisor signing the case off needs to see the
                issue and fail reason behind every remedial action, and on a case whose checks
                are all approved the collapse left the form with no numbered rows at all
                (project owner, 2026-09-11). Nothing on this form is an input, so a settled
                row is already read-only - what changes is only whether it is drawn.

                Approved as a whole, not action by action, which is the rule
                SignoffProgressPlugin now enforces server-side: the case leaves Awaiting
                Sign-off only once every action on the check has been decided.

                Two passes over the same small set - one case's actions, each with at most a
                handful of sign-offs - for the reason the Sign-off column already gives.
                Membership is tested against a string of ids rather than a list, because this
                Liquid has no set and `contains` on a delimited string is the shape the rest
                of the site already uses.
              {% endcomment %}
              {% assign ot_settled = '' %}
              {% assign ot_seen = '' %}
              {% assign ot_settled_note = '' %}
              {% assign ot_checks = 0 %}
              {% for a in rows %}
                {% assign rid = a.al_reviewinstanceid.id %}
                {% capture rprobe %}|{{ rid }}|{% endcapture %}
                {% unless ot_seen contains rprobe %}
                  {% capture ot_seen %}{{ ot_seen }}{{ rprobe }}{% endcapture %}
                  {% assign ot_checks = ot_checks | plus: 1 %}
                  {% assign ot_all_ok = true %}
                  {% assign ot_when = null %}
                  {% for b in rows %}
                    {% if b.al_reviewinstanceid.id == rid %}
                      {% assign bl = null %}
                      {% if signoffs %}{% for s in signoffs.results.entities %}{% if bl == null and s.al_remediationactionid.id == b.al_remediationactionid %}{% assign bl = s %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
                      {% if bl and bl.al_signoffdecision.value == 120910720 %}
                        {% if ot_when == null %}{% assign ot_when = bl.al_signedoffon %}{% endif %}
                      {% else %}
                        {% assign ot_all_ok = false %}
                      {% endif %}
                    {% endif %}
                  {% endfor %}
                  {% if ot_all_ok %}
                    {% capture ot_settled %}{{ ot_settled }}{{ rprobe }}{% endcapture %}
                    {% capture ot_settled_note %}{{ ot_settled_note }}{% if ot_settled_note != '' %}; {% endif %}{{ a.al_reviewinstanceid.name | default: 'an earlier check' | escape }} approved{% if ot_when %} {{ ot_when | date: 'dd MMM yyyy' }}{% endif %}{% endcapture %}
                  {% endif %}
                {% endunless %}
              {% endfor %}

              {% comment %}
                ot_checks is kept because the heading below reads differently on a one-check
                case, and the earlier reset of ot_settled on such a case is gone with the
                collapse it existed for: a single approved check should still say so.
              {% endcomment %}

              {% assign ot_group = '' %}
              {% for a in rows %}
                {% assign latest = null %}
                {% if signoffs %}{% for s in signoffs.results.entities %}{% if latest == null and s.al_remediationactionid.id == a.al_remediationactionid %}{% assign latest = s %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
                {% if latest %}
                  {% if latest.al_signoffdecision.value == 120910721 %}{% assign any_rejected = true %}{% assign all_approved = false %}{% endif %}
                {% else %}
                  {% assign all_approved = false %}
                {% endif %}
                {% if form_source == null and a.al_clientcontactrequired %}{% assign form_source = a %}{% endif %}
                {% if a.al_completedon %}
                  {% if latest_adviser == null or a.al_completedon > latest_adviser.al_completedon %}{% assign latest_adviser = a %}{% endif %}
                {% endif %}
                {% comment %}
                  al_description carries the whole list Remediation.Describe built: a heading,
                  one "- item" line per thing the checker marked down, then the checker's
                  observation. The standing sentence Describe ends with is dropped rather than
                  shown: it said the same thing under every row of every case, and both halves of
                  it are on the page in their own right now - the outcome as the remediation's
                  Outcome above, and what to do about it as the row the adviser answers
                  (project owner, 2026-09-10). It stays in al_description, which is the record
                  Dataverse keeps and the only place the outcome is written down.
                  observation and the standing sentence. The agreed form numbers those items one
                  to a row, so they are split back out here and the rest is shown once, under
                  them.

                  Every filter used is one this site already relies on elsewhere, and the
                  arguments are the shapes it already passes: no two-argument truncate and no
                  multi-character split, both of which this Liquid rejects. The line break is
                  turned into a single character first (newline_to_br writes a tag this Liquid
                  understands whatever the stored line endings are) so the split is on one
                  character. A line is an item when putting "- " back in front of it with its
                  first "- " removed reproduces it - true only when the "- " was at the front,
                  so "AML - No CRA" is an item's text, not a bullet.

                  If any of that does not take, ot_count stays 0 and the action falls back to
                  the single row it drew before. Inline rather than in a snippet of its own: an
                  included template gets its own scope, so these assigns would not come back.
                  The same block is in OT Case Detail.
                {% endcomment %}
                {% comment %}
                  The aggregates above are still read from every action, settled or not - they
                  describe the case, and a check that is finished is still part of it. Only the
                  drawing stops here, which is what "collapses away" means.
                {% endcomment %}
                {% capture rprobe %}|{{ a.al_reviewinstanceid.id }}|{% endcapture %}
                {% assign is_settled = false %}
                {% if ot_settled contains rprobe %}{% assign is_settled = true %}{% endif %}
                {% comment %}
                  The check these rows belong to, named once above them. A Tax-then-AQS case
                  can have both legs live at once only if one was sent back, so this is usually
                  a single heading - but when it is not, the two remediations have to be
                  telling apart on sight.
                {% endcomment %}
                {% assign this_group = a.al_reviewinstanceid.name | default: 'This check' %}
                {% if this_group != ot_group %}
                  {% assign ot_group = this_group %}
                  <tr class="ot-remedial-group{% if is_settled %} ot-remedial-group--settled{% endif %}">
                    <th scope="colgroup" colspan="8">
                      {{ ot_group | escape }}{% if is_settled %}<span class="ot-remedial-form__note"> · every action approved, closed</span>{% endif %}
                    </th>
                  </tr>
                {% endif %}
                {% assign ot_flat = a.al_description | newline_to_br | replace: '<br />', '|' | replace: '<br>', '|' %}
                {% assign ot_lines = ot_flat | split: '|' %}
                {% assign ot_count = 0 %}
                {% capture ot_note %}{% for l in ot_lines %}{% assign line = l | strip %}{% assign rest = line | remove_first: '- ' %}{% assign rebuilt = '- ' | append: rest %}{% if rebuilt == line %}{% assign ot_count = ot_count | plus: 1 %}{% elsif line != '' and line != 'Issues found on the check:' %}{% unless line contains 'Raised automatically when the review was submitted' %}{% unless line contains 'Review the file and record what you have put right' %}{{ line }} {% endunless %}{% endunless %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endcapture %}
                {% assign ot_note = ot_note | strip %}
                {% if ot_count > 0 %}
                  {% assign ot_shown = 0 %}
                  {% for l in ot_lines %}
                    {% assign line = l | strip %}{% assign rest = line | remove_first: '- ' %}{% assign rebuilt = '- ' | append: rest %}
                    {% if rebuilt == line %}
                      {% assign ot_shown = ot_shown | plus: 1 %}
                      {% assign row_no = row_no | plus: 1 %}
                      <tr>
                        <td>{{ row_no }}</td>
                        <td>{{ rest | escape }}</td>
                        {% if ot_shown == 1 %}
                          {% comment %}
                            The adviser answers in this cell. It used to be static text with
                            the editor behind a details/summary dropdown in a row of its own
                            (project owner, 2026-09-10: "the dropdown should be removed and
                            users should be able to answer directly in the remedial action
                            field"), which is also what the paper form draws - one cell per
                            issue, written in.

                            Rendered as a field only for an action assigned to the signed-in
                            contact that is not Completed. Presentation only: the
                            Contact-scoped table permission is what decides whose action can
                            be written (AD-069) and CompleteRemediationPlugin re-checks the
                            status and the response server-side.
                          {% endcomment %}
                          {% if user and a.al_assignedcontactid.id == user.id and a.al_actionstatus.value != 120910602 %}
                            <td rowspan="{{ ot_count }}" class="ot-response-cell" data-ot-response data-action-id="{{ a.al_remediationactionid }}" data-row-no="{{ row_no }}">
                              <label class="ot-visually-hidden" for="ot-response-{{ a.al_remediationactionid }}">Remedial action for issue {{ row_no }}</label>
                              <textarea id="ot-response-{{ a.al_remediationactionid }}"
                                        rows="4"
                                        class="ot-response-cell__text"
                                        data-ot-response-text>{{ a.al_adviserresponse | escape }}</textarea>
                            </td>
                          {% else %}
                            <td rowspan="{{ ot_count }}">{{ a.al_adviserresponse | default: '—' | escape | newline_to_br }}</td>
                          {% endif %}
                          <td rowspan="{{ ot_count }}">{{ a.al_assignedcontactid.name | default: c.al_advisername | default: 'Unassigned' | escape }}</td>
                          <td rowspan="{{ ot_count }}">{{ a.al_duedate | date: 'dd MMM yyyy' | default: '—' }}</td>
                          <td rowspan="{{ ot_count }}" data-ot-row-status="{{ a.al_remediationactionid }}">{% include 'OT Status Badge' status: a.al_actionstatus.label %}</td>
                          <td rowspan="{{ ot_count }}">
                            {% assign clock_start = a.al_clockstartedon | default: a.createdon %}
                            <span class="ot-age"
                                  data-ot-age
                                  data-opened="{{ clock_start | date: 'yyyy-MM-dd' }}"
                                  data-created="{{ a.createdon | date: 'yyyy-MM-dd' }}"
                                  data-completed="{{ a.al_completedon | date: 'yyyy-MM-dd' }}">—</span>
                          </td>
                          <td rowspan="{{ ot_count }}" data-ot-row-decision="{{ a.al_remediationactionid }}">
                            {% if latest %}
                              {{ latest.al_signoffdecision.label | escape }} {{ latest.al_signedoffon | date: 'dd MMM yyyy' }}
                            {% elsif a.al_completedon %}
                              Adviser completed {{ a.al_completedon | date: 'dd MMM yyyy' }}; awaiting supervisor
                            {% else %}
                              —
                            {% endif %}
                          </td>
                        {% endif %}
                      </tr>
                    {% endif %}
                  {% endfor %}
                  {% comment %}
                    The checker's observation is not drawn under the rows (project owner,
                    2026-09-10). ot_note is still captured because the same loop counts the
                    items, and ot_count is what decides the branch above.
                  {% endcomment %}
                {% else %}
                  {% assign row_no = row_no | plus: 1 %}
                  <tr>
                    <td>{{ row_no }}</td>
                    <td>—</td>
                    <td>{{ a.al_adviserresponse | default: '—' | escape | newline_to_br }}</td>
                    <td>{{ a.al_assignedcontactid.name | default: c.al_advisername | default: 'Unassigned' | escape }}</td>
                    <td>{{ a.al_duedate | date: 'dd MMM yyyy' | default: '—' }}</td>
                    <td>{% include 'OT Status Badge' status: a.al_actionstatus.label %}</td>
                    <td>
                      {% assign clock_start = a.al_clockstartedon | default: a.createdon %}
                      <span class="ot-age"
                            data-ot-age
                            data-opened="{{ clock_start | date: 'yyyy-MM-dd' }}"
                            data-created="{{ a.createdon | date: 'yyyy-MM-dd' }}"
                            data-completed="{{ a.al_completedon | date: 'yyyy-MM-dd' }}">—</span>
                    </td>
                    <td>
                      {% if latest %}
                        {{ latest.al_signoffdecision.label | escape }} {{ latest.al_signedoffon | date: 'dd MMM yyyy' }}
                      {% elsif a.al_completedon %}
                        Adviser completed {{ a.al_completedon | date: 'dd MMM yyyy' }}; awaiting supervisor
                      {% else %}
                        —
                      {% endif %}
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                {% endif %}
                {% comment %}
                  The adviser's half of the BR-008 loop (PP-12, FR-020, FR-021), inline rather
                  than on a page of its own so the form and the response live together.

                  Rendered only for an action assigned to the signed-in contact that is still
                  Open or In progress. Keyed on the status, not on al_completedon: a rejected
                  sign-off reopens the action to In progress but deliberately keeps the earlier
                  al_completedon (OD-018, SignoffProgressPlugin.ReopenedAction), so a test on the
                  completion date hid this panel on every action sent back for rework and the
                  adviser had nowhere to respond. That is presentation, not a boundary: the
                  Contact-scoped table permission is what actually decides whose action can be
                  written (AD-069), and CompleteRemediationPlugin re-checks the status and the
                  response server-side.
                {% endcomment %}
              {% endfor %}

              {% comment %}
                The adviser's three answers and the Intelligent Office reference, asked ONCE
                for the whole remediation (project owner, 2026-09-10: "they should be for the
                overall remediation... the rows only need to record the remedial action for
                each issue").

                AD-107 raises one action per fail item, and these five columns live on the
                action row, so asking them in each row's panel asked an adviser with four
                issues the same four questions four times. There is no case-level row to hold
                them, so the answers are written to every one of this adviser's actions that
                is still open - see the script below - which keeps any action correct when
                read on its own, and survives an action being deleted, as dropoutcomeactions
                does.

                Completed actions are deliberately excluded from that list:
                RemediationResponseGuard refuses a response-column change once an action is
                Completed, because that is what the supervisor attested to (BR-008). So a
                later change reaches the actions still in flight and leaves the attested ones
                as they were signed off.

                They are drawn as the last rows of the same table (project owner, 2026-09-10:
                they belong within the table). The paper form prints them in a ruled block
                directly under the numbered rows, and putting them in the table is what makes
                that one grid rather than two that happen to sit near each other.
              {% endcomment %}
              {% assign answer_ids = '' %}
              {% assign answers_source = null %}
              {% comment %}
                The actions awaiting the supervisor. Collected here so the attestation is
                one button for the whole remediation rather than one per row (project owner,
                2026-09-10) - the T&C Manager attests to the remediation, and the paper form
                carries one supervisor signature, not one per numbered issue.
              {% endcomment %}
              {% assign signoff_ids = '' %}
              {% for a in rows %}
                {% if user and a.al_assignedcontactid.id == user.id and a.al_actionstatus.value != 120910602 %}
                  {% if answer_ids == '' %}{% assign answer_ids = a.al_remediationactionid %}{% else %}{% assign answer_ids = answer_ids | append: ',' | append: a.al_remediationactionid %}{% endif %}
                  {% if answers_source == null %}{% assign answers_source = a %}{% endif %}
                {% endif %}
                {% comment %}
                  Decided means APPROVED. A rejection reopens the action for rework and the
                  guard then accepts a second decision on it (SignoffGuardPlugin.AlreadySettled,
                  2026-09-12); counting the rejection row as the decision kept the reworked
                  action out of this panel, so the supervisor had no control to give it the
                  approval that would close the loop - the IO-300003 shape, reintroduced on
                  the page. 120910720 is Approved on al_signoffdecision.
                {% endcomment %}
                {% if a.al_completedon and a.al_actionstatus.value == 120910602 %}
                  {% assign has_decision = false %}
                  {% if signoffs %}{% for sg in signoffs.results.entities %}{% if sg.al_remediationactionid.id == a.al_remediationactionid and sg.al_signoffdecision.value == 120910720 %}{% assign has_decision = true %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
                  {% unless has_decision %}
                    {% if signoff_ids == '' %}{% assign signoff_ids = a.al_remediationactionid %}{% else %}{% assign signoff_ids = signoff_ids | append: ',' | append: a.al_remediationactionid %}{% endif %}
                  {% endunless %}
                {% endif %}
              {% endfor %}
              {% if answers_source == null %}{% assign answers_source = form_source %}{% endif %}
              {% comment %}
                And a source for the read-only cells in those same rows, for a reader who is
                not the adviser: the first action, so the cell shows the recorded label or a
                dash rather than nothing. Read with a loop, never entities[0]. It follows
                answers_source deliberately - a checked radio must come from an action that
                actually carries an answer, not from the first row on the case.
              {% endcomment %}
              {% if form_source == null %}{% for a in rows %}{% if form_source == null %}{% assign form_source = a %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}

              <tr class="ot-form-rows__lead">
                <th scope="row" colspan="2">Client contact required?</th>
                <td colspan="2">
                  {% if answer_ids != '' %}
                    <span class="ot-opts" data-ot-form-answers data-action-ids="{{ answer_ids }}"
                          data-user-name="{{ user.fullname | escape }}">
                      <label><input type="radio" name="ot-form-cc" value="120910793" data-ot-fq="clientcontact"{% if answers_source.al_clientcontactrequired.value == 120910793 %} checked{% endif %} /> Yes</label>
                      <label><input type="radio" name="ot-form-cc" value="120910794" data-ot-fq="clientcontact"{% if answers_source.al_clientcontactrequired.value == 120910794 %} checked{% endif %} /> No</label>
                      <label><input type="radio" name="ot-form-cc" value="120910795" data-ot-fq="clientcontact"{% if answers_source.al_clientcontactrequired.value == 120910795 %} checked{% endif %} /> Potentially</label>
                    </span>
                  {% else %}
                    {{ form_source.al_clientcontactrequired.label | default: '—' | escape }}
                  {% endif %}
                </td>
                <th scope="row" colspan="2">Recheck required?</th>
                <td colspan="2">
                  {% if answer_ids != '' %}
                    <span class="ot-opts">
                      <label><input type="radio" name="ot-form-rc" value="120910796" data-ot-fq="recheck"{% if answers_source.al_recheckrequired.value == 120910796 %} checked{% endif %} /> Yes</label>
                      <label><input type="radio" name="ot-form-rc" value="120910797" data-ot-fq="recheck"{% if answers_source.al_recheckrequired.value == 120910797 %} checked{% endif %} /> No</label>
                    </span>
                  {% else %}
                    {{ form_source.al_recheckrequired.label | default: '—' | escape }}
                  {% endif %}
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" colspan="2">Do the remedial actions change the advice?</th>
                <td colspan="2">
                  {% if answer_ids != '' %}
                    <span class="ot-opts">
                      <label><input type="radio" name="ot-form-ca" value="120910798" data-ot-fq="changesadvice"{% if answers_source.al_changesadvice.value == 120910798 %} checked{% endif %} /> Yes</label>
                      <label><input type="radio" name="ot-form-ca" value="120910799" data-ot-fq="changesadvice"{% if answers_source.al_changesadvice.value == 120910799 %} checked{% endif %} /> No</label>
                    </span>
                  {% else %}
                    {{ form_source.al_changesadvice.label | default: '—' | escape }}
                  {% endif %}
                </td>
                <th scope="row" colspan="2">All remedial actions checked and approved?</th>
                <td colspan="2" data-ot-approved-cell>{% if all_approved %}Yes{% elsif any_rejected %}No{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        {% if ot_settled_note != '' %}
          {% comment %}
            Which checks are closed and when they were approved, under the table that now
            draws their rows. It read "Settled and not shown" while those rows were collapsed;
            they are shown, so it says what was approved and leaves the rows to speak.
          {% endcomment %}
          <p class="ot-filters__summary">
            Closed: {{ ot_settled_note }}. Every action on
            {% if ot_settled_note contains ';' %}those checks was{% else %}that check was{% endif %}
            approved, and {% if ot_settled_note contains ';' %}their rows are{% else %}its rows are{% endif %}
            above for reference.
          </p>
        {% endif %}

        {% assign outcome = null %}
        {% for o in caseoutcomes.results.entities %}{% if outcome == null %}{% assign outcome = o %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}

        {% comment %}
          The rest of the paper form, read-only: the regraded outcome with the note that says
          whose signature it is, and below it the two sign-offs as signatory and date.

          The four answers are NOT repeated here. They close the actions table above, where
          they are radios for this adviser and the recorded label for everyone else, so a
          copy in this block drew the same four questions twice - an editable set and a grey
          read-only set beneath it. One rendering, which already covers both readers.

          Reported rather than collected: the regrade is al_RegradeCase and the supervisor's
          decision is a create on al_signoff, so inputs here would be a second write path on
          columns that already have a permissioned one.
        {% endcomment %}
        <table class="ot-remedial-form__grid">
          <caption class="ot-visually-hidden">Regraded outcome for this remediation</caption>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">
                Regraded outcome
                <span class="ot-remedial-form__note">(for potential harms / insufficient evidence — the supervisor signs this off)</span>
              </th>
              <td colspan="3" data-ot-regraded-cell>
                {% comment %}
                  Through OT Outcome Label, not `.label` directly. The platform does not
                  always supply a formatted value for an option set, which renders as an
                  empty string rather than as an error - so `(% if outcome.al_finaloutcome %)`
                  passes on the object, `.label` yields nothing, and the cell draws blank
                  while the row plainly carries Pass. Reported 2026-09-11 on IO-300005, whose
                  regrade had recorded correctly and read as though it had not. The include
                  carries the numeric fallback for exactly this, which is the reason it
                  exists; only the case list was using it.

                  Passed `final` alone, so this stays the REGRADED outcome and does not fall
                  back to the initial grade the way the shared precedence rule does. Neither
                  template defines `initial` or `final`, so nothing leaks into the include.
                {% endcomment %}
                {% capture regraded_label %}{% include 'OT Outcome Label' final: outcome.al_finaloutcome %}{% endcapture %}
                {% assign regraded_label = regraded_label | strip %}
                {% comment %}
                  An empty cell used to read as a fault. It was reported as one on case
                  254397454, whose regrade "did not show": the case is Tax only, and a
                  remediated Tax-only case carries no al_outcome row at all (AD-055), so
                  there was never a grade to show and a bare dash could not say so.

                  Three states, each said plainly: the grade where one is recorded; "not
                  applicable" with the reason where the route means none can ever exist;
                  and "not recorded yet" where a grade is owed but has not been set - a
                  supervisor who left the sign-off dropdown on "Leave for a separate
                  regrade" is looking at that one, and it is genuinely still outstanding.

                  The route is the test rather than the absence of the row, because the two
                  say different things: no row on a Tax-only case is by design, and no row
                  on a case that owes a grade is work not done.
                {% endcomment %}
                {% assign route_name = c['rt.al_name'] %}
                {% if regraded_label != '' %}{{ regraded_label | escape }}{% elsif route_name == 'Tax only' %}<span class="ot-remedial-form__note">Not applicable — a Tax-only case carries no advice quality grade</span>{% else %}<span class="ot-remedial-form__note">Not recorded yet</span>{% endif %}
                {% if outcome and outcome.al_regradedon %}<span class="ot-remedial-form__note">· {{ outcome.al_regradedon | date: 'dd MMM yyyy' }}</span>{% elsif outcome and outcome.al_finalisedon %}<span class="ot-remedial-form__note">· {{ outcome.al_finalisedon | date: 'dd MMM yyyy' }}</span>{% endif %}
              </td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <table class="ot-remedial-form__signoffs">
          <caption class="ot-visually-hidden">Sign-off</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Date</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">
                Supervisor sign-off
                <span class="ot-remedial-form__note">(complete remedial task in IO)</span>
              </th>
              {% comment %}
                The signatory sits between the decision and the date, the order the paper
                form reads them in. al_signedbyname is stamped by SignoffRequestPlugin from
                the contact whose own request column carried the decision, so it names the
                supervisor rather than the site's application user a portal write arrives as.
                A sign-off recorded before that column existed carries none and reads as
                decision and date alone - which is the most its row can honestly say.
              {% endcomment %}
              <td data-ot-supervisor-cell>{% if latest_supervisor %}{{ latest_supervisor.al_signoffdecision.label | escape }}{% if latest_supervisor.al_signedbyname and latest_supervisor.al_signedbyname != '' %}, {{ latest_supervisor.al_signedbyname | escape }}{% endif %}, {{ latest_supervisor.al_signedoffon | date: 'dd MMM yyyy' }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">
                Adviser sign-off
                <span class="ot-remedial-form__note">(complete remedial task in IO)</span>
              </th>
              <td data-ot-adviser-cell>{% if latest_adviser %}{{ latest_adviser.al_assignedcontactid.name | default: c.al_advisername | escape }}, {{ latest_adviser.al_completedon | date: 'dd MMM yyyy' }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        {% comment %}
          One button for the whole form (project owner, 2026-09-10). Each open action this
          adviser holds takes a single request carrying its own remedial action, the three
          answers, and the completion - so the form is signed as a form, the way the paper
          one is, rather than a row at a time.

          Offered only to the adviser holding open actions. The permission that decides
          whose action may be written is the Contact-scoped table permission (AD-069), and
          CompleteRemediationPlugin re-checks the status and the response; this is the
          affordance, not the boundary.
        {% endcomment %}
        {% comment %}
          The T&C Manager's half of the loop (PP-12, FR-023, BR-008), as one decision for
          the whole remediation. Every action still awaiting a supervisor takes the same
          decision and notes in one pass.

          Whether the signed-in user may actually attest is decided by the create permission
          on al_signoff, which binds the T&C Supervisor role alone - this renders for anyone
          and a user without the role is refused on save. Showing it is a worse experience
          than hiding it, but hiding it by role in Liquid would look like access control and
          enforce nothing (NFR-SEC-01).
        {% endcomment %}
        {% if signoff_ids != '' %}
          <div class="ot-form-submit" data-ot-signoff data-action-ids="{{ signoff_ids }}"
               data-user-name="{{ user.fullname | escape }}">
            <div class="ot-field">
              <label for="ot-decision">All remedial actions checked and approved?</label>
              <select id="ot-decision" data-ot-signoff-decision>
                <option value="">Choose…</option>
                <option value="120910720">Approved</option>
                <option value="120910721">Rejected</option>
              </select>
            </div>
            {% comment %}
              The final outcome, recorded as the approval is made (project owner, 2026-09-11,
              settling OD-041). Approving used to leave the case at Awaiting Recheck for a
              separate regrade on the panel below, and nothing prompted anyone to do it - so
              a remediated case sat there still showing the grade the check gave before the
              adviser put anything right, and never reached Closed or the export.

              Offered only where there is a graded outcome to override, the same condition the
              regrade panel uses: a remediated Tax-only case has no al_outcome row at all
              (AD-055) and MoveCase closes it without one.
            {% endcomment %}
            {% if outcome and outcome.al_initialoutcome %}
              <div class="ot-field" data-ot-signoff-grade-field>
                <label for="ot-signoff-outcome">Final outcome</label>
                <select id="ot-signoff-outcome" data-ot-signoff-outcome>
                  <option value="">Leave for a separate regrade</option>
                  <option value="120910710">Pass</option>
                  <option value="120910711">Pass with issues</option>
                  <option value="120910712">Insufficient evidence</option>
                  <option value="120910713">Potential harm</option>
                </select>
              </div>
            {% endif %}
            <div class="ot-field">
              <label for="ot-notes">Notes</label>
              <textarea id="ot-notes" rows="3" data-ot-signoff-notes></textarea>
            </div>
            <button type="button" class="ot-btn ot-btn--primary" data-ot-signoff-save>
              Sign off this remediation
            </button>
            <p class="ot-response__status" data-ot-signoff-status aria-live="polite"></p>
            <p class="ot-form-submit__hint">
              Records your decision against every remedial action awaiting sign-off. Notes
              are required when rejecting: the adviser needs to know what to put right
              (BR-008), and a rejection returns the actions to them.
            </p>
          </div>
        {% endif %}

        {% comment %}
          The regrade (OD-041, AD-031, BR-005, BR-007), beside the sign-off because that is
          where the paper form puts it — the supervisor's own signature line, immediately
          after the approval.

          Signing off does not regrade: approving every action moves the case to Awaiting
          Recheck, the state that exists precisely so the final outcome can then be set, and
          setting it is what closes the case. Until this was here the only way to do that was
          the Code App at /cases/:caseId/recheck, so a supervisor holding only the portal
          could not finish the case they had just approved.

          Offered when the case carries an outcome that has actually been graded: a regrade
          overrides a grade, so there has to be one, and a remediated Tax-only case (AD-055)
          has no outcome row at all. Whether the signed-in user may attest is decided
          server-side by RegradeRequestPlugin against the contact's web roles - this renders
          for anyone and a user without the T&C Supervisor role is refused on save, for the
          same reason the sign-off above does not hide itself: hiding it by role in Liquid
          would look like access control and enforce nothing (NFR-SEC-01).

          And offered only where the case has reached its recheck. Hiding by STATE is not
          the same act as hiding by role: the role question is who you are, which Liquid
          must not appear to decide, while this is whether the case has got to the step at
          all. Recording the final outcome IS the recheck (AD-057), so it means something
          in exactly two states - Awaiting Recheck, and Closed for the AD-031 correction of
          a case already finished. Before then the remedial actions are open and nobody has
          attested to any of them, so a grade would be a verdict on work not yet done.
          Reported on case 254398988, which took a Pass at Awaiting Remediation with all six
          of its actions unanswered; RegradeCasePlugin.EnsureCaseIsAtTheRecheck now refuses
          it server-side, and this branch is so the supervisor is not offered a control that
          would be refused. The status is read from the case, so the panel returns by itself
          the moment the last sign-off moves it.

          The four options are BR-005's, in BR-005's order, and the reason is mandatory
          (AD-031) - required in the page so the supervisor is told before the request goes,
          and required again in the plug-in because a page is not a boundary.
        {% endcomment %}
        {% assign ot_at_recheck = false %}
        {% if c.al_casestatus.value == 120910590 %}{% assign ot_at_recheck = true %}{% endif %}
        {% if c.al_casestatus.value == 120910591 %}{% assign ot_at_recheck = true %}{% endif %}
        {% if outcome and outcome.al_initialoutcome %}{% unless ot_at_recheck %}
          {% comment %}
            The same two grades the panel reports, said where the panel would have been. A
            case carrying a final outcome it should never have been offered - 254398988 does,
            from before the guard - says so here rather than hiding it.
          {% endcomment %}
          {% capture early_initial %}{% include 'OT Outcome Label' initial: outcome.al_initialoutcome %}{% endcapture %}
          {% assign early_initial = early_initial | strip %}
          {% capture early_final %}{% include 'OT Outcome Label' final: outcome.al_finaloutcome %}{% endcapture %}
          {% assign early_final = early_final | strip %}
          <div class="ot-form-submit">
            <h3 class="ot-form-submit__title">Regraded outcome</h3>
            <p class="ot-form-submit__hint">
              The initial outcome is
              <strong>{{ early_initial | default: 'not recorded' | escape }}</strong>{% if early_final != '' %},
              and a final outcome of <strong>{{ early_final | escape }}</strong> is recorded
              against it{% if outcome.al_regradedon %} from {{ outcome.al_regradedon | date: 'dd MMM yyyy' }}{% endif %}{% endif %}.
              This case is at <strong>{{ c.al_casestatus.label | default: 'an earlier step' | escape }}</strong>.
              The final outcome is the recheck decision, so it is recorded here once every
              remedial action above has been signed off and the case reaches Awaiting
              Recheck.
            </p>
          </div>
        {% endunless %}{% endif %}
        {% if outcome and outcome.al_initialoutcome and ot_at_recheck %}
          <div class="ot-form-submit" data-ot-regrade
               data-outcome-id="{{ outcome.al_outcomeid }}"
               data-row-version="{{ outcome.versionnumber }}">
            <h3 class="ot-form-submit__title">Regraded outcome</h3>
{% comment %}
              Both grades through OT Outcome Label rather than `.label`, for the reason the
              Regraded outcome cell above gives: an unformatted option set renders blank, so
              this hint read "The initial outcome was ." on a case that had one.
            {% endcomment %}
            {% capture initial_label %}{% include 'OT Outcome Label' initial: outcome.al_initialoutcome %}{% endcapture %}
            {% assign initial_label = initial_label | strip %}
            {% capture final_label %}{% include 'OT Outcome Label' final: outcome.al_finaloutcome %}{% endcapture %}
            {% assign final_label = final_label | strip %}
            <p class="ot-form-submit__hint" data-ot-regrade-hint>
              The initial outcome was
              <strong>{{ initial_label | default: 'not recorded' | escape }}</strong>{% if final_label != '' %},
              regraded to <strong>{{ final_label | escape }}</strong>{% if outcome.al_regradedon %}
              on {{ outcome.al_regradedon | date: 'dd MMM yyyy' }}{% endif %}{% endif %}. Recording a final
              outcome does not change it — both are kept (BR-007).
            </p>
            <div class="ot-field">
              <label for="ot-regrade-outcome">Final outcome</label>
              <select id="ot-regrade-outcome" data-ot-regrade-outcome>
                <option value="">Choose…</option>
                <option value="Pass">Pass</option>
                <option value="Pass with issues">Pass with issues</option>
                <option value="Insufficient evidence">Insufficient evidence</option>
                <option value="Potential harm">Potential harm</option>
              </select>
            </div>
            <div class="ot-field">
              <label for="ot-regrade-reason">Reason <span class="ot-field__required">(required)</span></label>
              <textarea id="ot-regrade-reason" rows="3" data-ot-regrade-reason></textarea>
            </div>
            <button type="button" class="ot-btn ot-btn--primary" data-ot-regrade-save>
              Record the final outcome
            </button>
            <p class="ot-response__status" data-ot-regrade-status aria-live="polite"></p>
            <p class="ot-form-submit__hint">
              The initial outcome is kept whatever you record here (BR-007), and the reason
              is written to the case's audit history (AD-031). A case waiting at Awaiting
              Recheck is closed by this.
            </p>
          </div>
        {% endif %}

        {% if answer_ids != '' %}
          <div class="ot-form-submit">
            <button type="button" class="ot-btn" data-ot-form-draft>
              Save draft
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="ot-btn ot-btn--primary" data-ot-form-submit>
              Save and sign off this remediation
            </button>
            <p class="ot-response__status" data-ot-form-status aria-live="polite"></p>
            <p class="ot-form-submit__hint">
              Save draft keeps what you have written without signing anything off. Save and
              sign off records every remedial action above, your three answers, and your
              sign-off, and sends the remediation to your supervisor.
            </p>
          </div>
        {% endif %}

      {% else %}
        {% include 'OT Empty State' title: 'No remediation actions' message: 'Nothing has been raised against this case.' %}
      {% endif %}
      </div>
    </section>
  {% endif %}

{% endif %}

<script>
  /*
   * Working-day ageing for the BR-010 remediation clock (OD-018).
   *
   * Mirrors app/src/lib/workingDays.ts: Monday to Friday, the opening day counts as
   * day 1, bank holidays are not deducted. An action that has completed is aged to its
   * completion date, so a finished action stops ticking.
   *
   * data-opened is the start of the CURRENT period, which a rejected sign-off resets
   * (OD-018). data-created is the original start, so where the two differ the period the
   * rejection ended is shown beside the current one rather than added to it — an action
   * back with the adviser is on a fresh ten days, and the earlier round is history, not
   * a debt against the new one.
   *
   * Input is a yyyy-MM-dd calendar date the server already resolved, so nothing here
   * converts a timezone. Each date is pinned to midday UTC before arithmetic, which is
   * what stops a day slipping when the browser sits in another region.
   */
  (function () {
    'use strict';

    var THRESHOLD = 10;

    function midday(text) {
      if (!text) { return null; }
      var parts = /^(\d{4})-(\d{2})-(\d{2})$/.exec(text);
      if (!parts) { return null; }
      return new Date(Date.UTC(+parts[1], +parts[2] - 1, +parts[3], 12, 0, 0));
    }

    function workingDaysBetween(from, to) {
      if (to.getTime() < from.getTime()) { return 0; }
      var count = 0;
      var cursor = new Date(from.getTime());
      while (cursor.getTime() <= to.getTime()) {
        var day = cursor.getUTCDay();
        if (day >= 1 && day <= 5) { count += 1; }
        cursor.setUTCDate(cursor.getUTCDate() + 1);
      }
      return count;
    }

    var now = new Date();
    var today = new Date(Date.UTC(now.getFullYear(), now.getMonth(), now.getDate(), 12, 0, 0));

    var cells = document.querySelectorAll('[data-ot-age]');
    for (var i = 0; i < cells.length; i += 1) {
      var cell = cells[i];
      var opened = midday(cell.getAttribute('data-opened'));
      if (!opened) { continue; }

      var completed = midday(cell.getAttribute('data-completed'));
      var age = workingDaysBetween(opened, completed || today);

      cell.textContent = age + (age === 1 ? ' working day' : ' working days');

      // A clock that has been reset carries an earlier period. Show it, because a case
      // that has been round twice is not the same as one on its first ten days, and the
      // adviser and the T&C Manager both need to see that it went back.
      var created = midday(cell.getAttribute('data-created'));
      if (created && created.getTime() < opened.getTime()) {
        var previous = workingDaysBetween(created, opened);
        var note = document.createElement('span');
        note.className = 'ot-age__previous';
        note.textContent = ' (reworked; previous period ' + previous +
          (previous === 1 ? ' working day)' : ' working days)');
        cell.appendChild(note);
        cell.setAttribute('title',
          'Sent back after sign-off. The ten-working-day threshold runs from the restart (OD-018).');
      }

      if (!completed && age > THRESHOLD) {
        cell.classList.add('ot-age--breached');
        var existing = cell.getAttribute('title');
        cell.setAttribute('title',
          (existing ? existing + ' ' : '') + 'Past the ten-working-day threshold (BR-010).');
      }
    }
  })();
</script>

<script>
  /*
   * Bringing the rows up to date after a write, without asking the server again.
   *
   * Every write on this page PATCHes a trigger column and a synchronous plug-in does the
   * real work on OTHER tables - al_remediationaction, al_signoff, al_outcome,
   * al_outcomecase. Those rows are committed by the time the PATCH returns, but the portal
   * did not write them, so its render cache is not invalidated by the write path and learns
   * through Dataverse change tracking (AD-094), which is polled. A reload inside that window
   * re-draws the state the page already had, under a success message - which is what
   * "the sign-off does not show the updates" was, reported on case 254398988 whose six
   * actions were Completed and approved in Dataverse while the page kept showing them Open.
   *
   * So the page stops reloading and says what it knows instead. It knows exactly what it
   * just asked for and got a 2xx on, which is enough for the two cells a write changes: the
   * status of the action, and the decision standing against it. Anything it cannot know for
   * certain - the supervisor's panel appearing, the case moving on - is left to a reload the
   * reader asks for, with the cache caveat attached, rather than one the page springs.
   *
   * Deliberately not innerHTML: the labels come from a select the user just used, and text
   * that reaches the DOM as text cannot be anything else.
   */
  window.otRemediationRows = (function () {
    'use strict';

    var MONTHS = ['Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar', 'Apr', 'May', 'Jun',
                  'Jul', 'Aug', 'Sep', 'Oct', 'Nov', 'Dec'];

    // 'dd MMM yyyy', matching the Liquid date filter the cells are rendered with, so a
    // row this rewrites cannot be told apart from a row the server drew.
    function today() {
      var now = new Date();
      var day = now.getDate();
      return (day < 10 ? '0' + day : String(day)) + ' ' + MONTHS[now.getMonth()] + ' ' + now.getFullYear();
    }

    function cells(attribute, ids) {
      var found = [];
      for (var i = 0; i < ids.length; i += 1) {
        var id = (ids[i] || '').replace(/^\s+|\s+$/g, '');
        if (!id) { continue; }
        var cell = document.querySelector('[' + attribute + '="' + id + '"]');
        if (cell) { found.push(cell); }
      }
      return found;
    }

    function setText(cell, text) {
      cell.textContent = text;
    }

    /*
     * The badge markup OT Status Badge produces for a label, mirroring that template's
     * cascade in its own order. Mirrored rather than improved - a cell the page rewrites has
     * to look like the ones around it, and choosing a nicer colour here would make the two
     * disagree. Anything it does not recognise falls to the default, as the include does.
     *
     * The labels this page can put through it: 'Completed' (no keyword, so the default
     * waiting), 'In progress' (active), and 'Closed', which a regrade leaves the case in.
     */
    function badgeClass(label) {
      var name = String(label || '').toLowerCase();
      if (name === '') { return 'none'; }
      if (name.indexOf('potential harm') !== -1) { return 'harm'; }
      if (name.indexOf('insufficient') !== -1) { return 'insufficient'; }
      if (name.indexOf('issues') !== -1) { return 'issues'; }
      if (name.indexOf('pass') !== -1) { return 'pass'; }
      if (name.indexOf('closed') !== -1 || name.indexOf('no check required') !== -1) { return 'closed'; }
      if (name.indexOf('fail') !== -1 || name.indexOf('blocked') !== -1 || name.indexOf('overdue') !== -1) { return 'blocked'; }
      if (name.indexOf('progress') !== -1 || name.indexOf('assigned') !== -1 || name.indexOf('submitted') !== -1) { return 'active'; }
      return 'waiting';
    }

    function badge(cell, label) {
      cell.textContent = '';
      var span = document.createElement('span');
      span.className = 'ot-badge ot-badge--' + badgeClass(label);
      span.textContent = label;
      cell.appendChild(span);
    }

    return {
      /* The adviser has signed the form off: every action they answered is now Completed
         and waiting on the supervisor. */
      completed: function (ids) {
        var status = cells('data-ot-row-status', ids);
        for (var i = 0; i < status.length; i += 1) { badge(status[i], 'Completed'); }

        var decision = cells('data-ot-row-decision', ids);
        for (var j = 0; j < decision.length; j += 1) {
          setText(decision[j], 'Adviser completed ' + today() + '; awaiting supervisor');
        }
      },

      /*
       * The supervisor has decided. The decision cell carries the label and the date, the
       * same two things the server renders there from the al_signoff row.
       *
       * A rejection also moves the action: SignoffProgressPlugin puts it back to In
       * progress for the rework (AD-125), so the status cell has to move with it or the
       * page would show a rejected action still sitting at Completed. An approval leaves
       * the action Completed, which is what the cell already says.
       */
      decided: function (ids, label, rejected) {
        var decision = cells('data-ot-row-decision', ids);
        for (var i = 0; i < decision.length; i += 1) {
          setText(decision[i], label + ' ' + today());
        }

        if (!rejected) { return; }

        var status = cells('data-ot-row-status', ids);
        for (var j = 0; j < status.length; j += 1) { badge(status[j], 'In progress'); }
      },

      /*
       * The adviser has signed the form off, so the row that reports who last completed one
       * says so. Certain: the form completes the signed-in adviser's own open actions, and
       * the cell names that person and the date.
       */
      adviserCompleted: function (name) {
        var cell = document.querySelector('[data-ot-adviser-cell]');
        if (cell) {
          setText(cell, (name ? name + ', ' : '') + today());
        }
      },

      /*
       * The supervisor has decided, so the row that reports the last decision says so, and
       * the "All remedial actions checked and approved?" cell moves with it.
       *
       * Both are certain. The panel signs off EVERY action awaiting a decision on this case
       * in one go, so after an approval every action is approved and after a rejection one
       * is rejected - which is exactly what the cell is derived from server-side.
       */
      supervisorDecided: function (label, name, rejected) {
        var cell = document.querySelector('[data-ot-supervisor-cell]');
        if (cell) {
          setText(cell, label + (name ? ', ' + name : '') + ', ' + today());
        }

        var approved = document.querySelector('[data-ot-approved-cell]');
        if (approved) {
          setText(approved, rejected ? 'No' : 'Yes');
        }
      },

      /*
       * Where the case went is the server's to decide, and the page must not guess it.
       *
       * Completing or approving can move a case to Awaiting Sign-off, Awaiting Recheck,
       * Closed, or back to Queued where the route still owes another discipline (OD-038) -
       * and which one depends on rules this page does not hold. So the badge is not rewritten
       * with a guess; it is marked as possibly out of date, which is the honest thing a page
       * can say about a value it knows may have changed and cannot recompute. A regrade is
       * the exception and sets Closed outright, because there the outcome is certain.
       */
      caseStatusMayHaveMoved: function () {
        var status = document.querySelector('[data-ot-case-status]');
        if (!status || status.querySelector('[data-ot-stale]')) { return; }
        var note = document.createElement('span');
        note.className = 'ot-remedial-form__note';
        note.setAttribute('data-ot-stale', '');
        note.textContent = ' \u00b7 may have moved, reload to confirm';
        status.appendChild(note);
      },

      /*
       * The final outcome has just been recorded, so the two cells that report it elsewhere
       * on the page have to move with it.
       *
       * The panel's own hint said so from the moment the reload was dropped, but the
       * Regraded outcome cell in the table above and the case's status badge in the heading
       * are server-rendered and kept saying "Not recorded yet" and "Awaiting Recheck" while
       * Dataverse held Pass and Closed. Reported on IO-300001 on 2026-09-13, whose regrade
       * had succeeded in full at 18:14:01. Removing a reload obliges the page to draw what
       * the reload used to fetch, and this is the half that was missed.
       *
       * Closed is certain rather than assumed: the panel is only drawn at Awaiting Recheck
       * or at Closed (AD-127), a regrade closes the first, and the second is already there.
       */
      regraded: function (label) {
        var cell = document.querySelector('[data-ot-regraded-cell]');
        if (cell) {
          // The grade, then the regraded-on date as its own note - the two parts the server
          // renders into this cell, in that order, so the rewritten cell matches it.
          cell.textContent = label + ' ';
          var when = document.createElement('span');
          when.className = 'ot-remedial-form__note';
          when.textContent = '\u00b7 ' + today();
          cell.appendChild(when);
        }

        var status = document.querySelector('[data-ot-case-status]');
        if (status) {
          // badge() clears the cell, which takes any "may have moved" marker with it. The
          // case status is no longer uncertain: a regrade from this panel closes the case.
          badge(status, 'Closed');
        }
      },

      /*
       * The case status as Dataverse has just reported it, replacing whatever the server
       * rendered from cache. Certain, because the caller read it from the Web API rather
       * than deriving it - so it clears the "may have moved" marker the same way `regraded`
       * does, and for the same reason.
       */
      caseStatusIs: function (label) {
        var status = document.querySelector('[data-ot-case-status]');
        if (!status || !label) { return; }
        badge(status, label);
      },

      /*
       * The reload the reader asks for. The page cannot draw the parts that need a server
       * render - the supervisor's panel after an adviser sign-off, the regrade panel after
       * the case reaches recheck - so it offers the reload instead of timing one, and says
       * what may still be stale when it lands.
       */
      offerReload: function (after) {
        if (!after || after.parentNode.querySelector('[data-ot-reload]')) { return; }
        var button = document.createElement('button');
        button.type = 'button';
        button.className = 'ot-btn';
        button.setAttribute('data-ot-reload', '');
        button.textContent = 'Reload the page';
        button.addEventListener('click', function () { window.location.reload(); });
        after.parentNode.insertBefore(button, after.nextSibling);
      }
    };
  })();
</script>

<script>
  /*
   * The case status, re-read from Dataverse on every load (AD-133, answering AD-094).
   *
   * The badge above is server-rendered from a Liquid fetchxml result, and Power Pages serves
   * that from a cache the writes on this case never invalidate: a sign-off and a regrade are
   * made by plug-ins, not by the website, so the only record the site clears for itself is
   * the contact it PATCHed. Everything else waits on polled change tracking, inside a
   * fifteen-minute SLA.
   *
   * `otRemediationRows.regraded` already corrects the badge, and AD-131 marks it where the
   * page cannot recompute it - but both only in the browser session that made the write. Come
   * back to this page afterwards and the server renders the stale value again, with no marker
   * on it, because no write happened in THIS page load. A stale badge carrying no marker
   * reads as authoritative, which is the half AD-131 could not cover. Reported
   * on 254398988 on 2026-09-14: the case page said Closed and this page said Awaiting Recheck
   * at the same moment, the case having closed two minutes earlier. Two Liquid queries, two
   * cache entries, one refreshed and one not.
   *
   * So the page stops trusting its own render for this one value and asks Dataverse. The Web
   * API is not the Liquid render cache, which is the whole point of reading through it here.
   *
   * Progressive enhancement, exactly like every other write on this page: a failure, a
   * refusal, or a browser that never runs this leaves the server-rendered badge alone. A
   * stale badge is what we already have, so there is nothing to lose by failing quietly -
   * and nothing here is a permission decision the page is entitled to make (NFR-SEC-01).
   */
  (function () {
    'use strict';

    var status = document.querySelector('[data-ot-case-status]');
    if (!status) { return; }

    var caseId = status.getAttribute('data-ot-case-id');
    if (!caseId) { return; }

    var FORMATTED = '@OData.Community.Display.V1.FormattedValue';

    var request = new XMLHttpRequest();
    request.open('GET', '/_api/al_outcomecases(' + caseId + ')?$select=al_casestatus', true);
    request.setRequestHeader('Accept', 'application/json');
    // The label rather than the option-set number. Without this the response carries
    // al_casestatus as an integer and the page would have to keep its own copy of the
    // lifecycle's values - a second place for them to drift from CaseLifecycle.cs.
    request.setRequestHeader(
      'Prefer', 'odata.include-annotations="OData.Community.Display.V1.FormattedValue"');

    request.onreadystatechange = function () {
      if (request.readyState !== 4) { return; }
      if (request.status < 200 || request.status >= 300) { return; }

      var live;
      try {
        live = JSON.parse(request.responseText)['al_casestatus' + FORMATTED];
      } catch (e) {
        return;
      }

      if (!live) { return; }

      // Only when it actually differs, so a page that was already current is not rewritten -
      // the badge would render identically, but replacing it would also silently discard a
      // "may have moved" marker that a write in this session had put there for another
      // reason.
      var shown = (status.textContent || '').replace(/^\s+|\s+$/g, '');
      if (shown === live) { return; }

      if (window.otRemediationRows) {
        window.otRemediationRows.caseStatusIs(live);
      }
    };

    request.send();
  })();
</script>

<script>
  /*
   * The adviser's half of the BR-008 loop, as one form (PP-12, FR-020, FR-021).
   *
   * Path: this page -> PATCH al_remediationaction -> CompleteRequestPlugin -> Dataverse.
   * Same mechanic as the review submit (AD-073): the portal's Web API cannot call an
   * action, so the page writes allowlisted columns and a synchronous plug-in does the work.
   *
   * One button for the whole form (project owner, 2026-09-10: "all the saves and sign offs
   * need to be actioned by a single button at the end of the form"). Each of this adviser's
   * open actions takes ONE request carrying its own remedial action, the three answers that
   * belong to the remediation as a whole, and the completion trigger - so an action can
   * never be marked complete with a response that failed to save, and the answers cannot
   * land on some rows and not others because a later request failed.
   *
   * A failure on any row stops the rest: the button reports which one and nothing further
   * is sent, so a half-signed form is something the adviser can see rather than discover.
   *
   * Progressive enhancement only. The status transition, the mandatory response and the
   * audit event are all enforced server-side (NFR-SEC-01).
   */
  (function () {
    'use strict';

    var submit = document.querySelector('[data-ot-form-submit]');
    var draft = document.querySelector('[data-ot-form-draft]');
    if (!submit) { return; }

    var status = document.querySelector('[data-ot-form-status]');
    var cells = document.querySelectorAll('[data-ot-response]');

    /*
     * The server's own words, out of the response body.
     *
     * The body is an OData error object, so the message has to be read out of it rather than
     * scanned for in the raw text: a prefix found by indexOf and taken to the end of the
     * string carries the JSON tail with it, which is why the branches below used to cut at
     * the next quote and why one of them did not and showed it.
     *
     * A body that will not parse is returned as it stands - it is still more than "something
     * went wrong" - and it is collapsed onto one line and capped, because an error line is
     * read on screen and the whole of a platform fault is not readable there.
     */
    function serverMessage(raw) {
      var text = String(raw || '').trim();
      if (!text) { return ''; }

      var message = text;
      try {
        var body = JSON.parse(text);
        var error = body && body.error ? body.error : body;
        if (error && error.innererror && error.innererror.message) {
          message = error.innererror.message;
        } else if (error && error.message) {
          message = error.message;
        }
      } catch (ignored) {
        // Not JSON. Keep the raw text.
      }

      message = String(message || '').replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim();
      if (message.length > 300) { message = message.substring(0, 300) + '...'; }
      return message;
    }

    // Shared with the form-answers script above, which is parsed first but only reads
    // this inside a request callback. One wording for a refusal, wherever it surfaced.
    function friendlyError(raw, httpStatus) {
      var text = serverMessage(raw);
      if (text.indexOf('CONFLICT:') !== -1) {
        return 'This action changed since you opened it. Reload the page and try again.';
      }
      if (text.indexOf('UNAUTHORIZED:') !== -1) {
        return 'You do not have permission to change this action.';
      }
      if (text.indexOf('PRECONDITION:') !== -1) {
        var idx = text.indexOf('PRECONDITION:');
        return text.substring(idx + 'PRECONDITION:'.length).trim();
      }
      if (text.indexOf('UNEXPECTED:') !== -1) {
        var unexpected = text.indexOf('UNEXPECTED:');
        return 'Nothing was saved. ' + text.substring(unexpected + 'UNEXPECTED:'.length).trim();
      }
      /*
       * A 403 is the permission chain, not a transient fault: the write on al_remediationaction
       * is Contact-scoped and bound to the Adviser Remediation and Planner roles (AD-069), so an
       * account without one of them is refused on every save and "try again" cannot help. The
       * generic line below hid exactly that on 2026-09-09.
       */
      if (httpStatus === 403) {
        return 'Your account is not allowed to change this action, so nothing was saved. Responding needs the '
          + 'Adviser Remediation or Planner role on your portal account, and the action has to be assigned to you. '
          + 'Ask an administrator to check both rather than retrying.';
      }
      if (httpStatus === 401) {
        return 'Your session was not accepted, so nothing was saved. Reload the page and sign in again.';
      }
      return 'That was not saved, and nothing has been changed. '
        + (text ? 'The server said: ' + text : 'The server gave no detail.')
        + (httpStatus ? ' (status ' + httpStatus + ')' : '');
    }

    window.otFriendlyError = friendlyError;

    function show(message, kind) {
      if (!status) { return; }
      status.textContent = message;
      status.className = 'ot-response__status ot-response__status--' + (kind || 'info');
      status.setAttribute('role', kind === 'error' ? 'alert' : 'status');
    }

    function answer(name) {
      var picked = document.querySelector('[data-ot-fq="' + name + '"]:checked');
      return picked ? Number(picked.value) : null;
    }

    /* Every row this adviser owns, with what they wrote in it. */
    function rows() {
      var found = [];
      for (var i = 0; i < cells.length; i += 1) {
        var text = cells[i].querySelector('[data-ot-response-text]');
        found.push({
          id: cells[i].getAttribute('data-action-id'),
          number: cells[i].getAttribute('data-row-no') || String(i + 1),
          text: text ? text.value : ''
        });
      }
      return found;
    }

    function busy(on) {
      submit.disabled = on;
      if (draft) { draft.disabled = on; }
    }

    // The viewer's own name, for the summary row that reports who last completed an action.
    // Rendered into the answers span rather than fetched, for the reason every other value
    // on this page is: the page already knows who is signed in.
    function viewerName() {
      var carrier = document.querySelector('[data-ot-form-answers]');
      return carrier ? (carrier.getAttribute('data-user-name') || '') : '';
    }

    // The actions this form answers, in the order the cells appear.
    function ids() {
      var found = [];
      for (var i = 0; i < cells.length; i += 1) {
        found.push(cells[i].getAttribute('data-action-id'));
      }
      return found;
    }

    /*
     * A signed-off form is not editable again from here. RemediationResponseGuard refuses a
     * response-column change once the action is Completed (BR-008 - that is what the
     * supervisor attests to), so leaving the fields live would invite an edit the server
     * would refuse. The draft button goes with them: there is no longer a draft to save.
     */
    function markSaved() {
      for (var i = 0; i < cells.length; i += 1) {
        var text = cells[i].querySelector('[data-ot-response-text]');
        if (text) { text.readOnly = true; }
      }

      var radios = document.querySelectorAll('[data-ot-fq]');
      for (var j = 0; j < radios.length; j += 1) { radios[j].disabled = true; }

      submit.disabled = true;
      if (draft) { draft.disabled = true; }
    }

    /*
     * markComplete false is a draft: it keeps what has been written and signs nothing off.
     *
     * A draft is deliberately not held to the completion rules - a half-filled form is the
     * point of it - so blank rows pass, and a question not yet answered is left out of the
     * payload rather than sent as null. Sending null would clear an answer the adviser had
     * already given, which is the opposite of saving.
     */
    function send(markComplete) {
      if (!window.shell || typeof window.shell.getTokenDeferred !== 'function') {
        show('This page did not load completely. Refresh and try again.', 'error');
        return;
      }

      var pending = rows();
      if (!pending.length) { return; }

      if (markComplete) {
        // Checked here only so the adviser is told before a round trip; the plug-in
        // refuses a completion with no response regardless.
        for (var i = 0; i < pending.length; i += 1) {
          if (!pending[i].text.replace(/^\s+|\s+$/g, '')) {
            show('Record the remedial action for issue ' + pending[i].number + ' before signing off.', 'error');
            return;
          }
        }

        if (answer('clientcontact') === null || answer('recheck') === null || answer('changesadvice') === null) {
          show('Answer the three questions for this remediation before signing off.', 'error');
          return;
        }
      }

      busy(true);
      show(markComplete ? 'Signing off...' : 'Saving draft...', 'info');

      window.shell.getTokenDeferred().done(function (token) {
        var index = 0;

        function next() {
          if (index >= pending.length) {
            if (!markComplete) {
              show('Draft saved.', 'success');
              busy(false);
              return;
            }

            /*
             * Confirmed in place, and no reload. The rows this wrote are the adviser's
             * remedial actions, which the page did not write itself - it PATCHed them and
             * CompleteRequestPlugin did the rest - so the portal's render cache does not
             * clear on this write and a reload inside the change-tracking window re-draws
             * every action Open under a success message. That is how a remediation fully
             * recorded in Dataverse read as one that had not saved (AD-094, AD-117, and
             * case 254398988 on 2026-09-13).
             *
             * The two cells the page can be certain of are brought up to date here; the
             * supervisor's panel needs a server render, so the reload is offered rather
             * than timed.
             */
            markSaved();
            if (window.otRemediationRows) {
              window.otRemediationRows.completed(ids());
              window.otRemediationRows.adviserCompleted(viewerName());
              window.otRemediationRows.caseStatusMayHaveMoved();
            }
            show('Signed off. ' + pending.length + ' remedial action'
              + (pending.length === 1 ? ' is' : 's are')
              + ' recorded against your three answers and sent to your supervisor.'
              + ' The rows above now show what was saved. Reload the page when you want the'
              + ' rest of it re-read, and if it still shows the old state the site cache has'
              + ' not caught up - try again in a moment.', 'success');
            if (window.otRemediationRows) {
              window.otRemediationRows.offerReload(status);
            }
            return;
          }

          var row = pending[index];
          var request = new XMLHttpRequest();
          request.open('PATCH', '/_api/al_remediationactions(' + row.id + ')', true);
          request.setRequestHeader('Content-Type', 'application/json');
          request.setRequestHeader('__RequestVerificationToken', token);

          request.onreadystatechange = function () {
            if (request.readyState !== 4) { return; }

            if (request.status >= 200 && request.status < 300) {
              index += 1;
              next();
              return;
            }

            show('Issue ' + row.number + ': ' + friendlyError(request.responseText, request.status), 'error');
            busy(false);
          };

          var payload = { al_adviserresponse: row.text };
          var cc = answer('clientcontact');
          var rc = answer('recheck');
          var ca = answer('changesadvice');
          if (cc !== null) { payload.al_clientcontactrequired = cc; }
          if (rc !== null) { payload.al_recheckrequired = rc; }
          if (ca !== null) { payload.al_changesadvice = ca; }
          if (markComplete) { payload.al_completerequested = true; }

          request.send(JSON.stringify(payload));
        }

        next();
      }).fail(function () {
        show('This page did not load completely. Refresh and try again.', 'error');
        busy(false);
      });
    }

    submit.addEventListener('click', function () { send(true); });
    if (draft) { draft.addEventListener('click', function () { send(false); }); }
  })();
</script>

<script>
  /*
   * T&C attestation (PP-12, FR-023, BR-008).
   *
   * Path: this page -> PATCH contact.al_signoffrequest -> SignoffRequestPlugin -> al_signoff
   *       -> SignoffGuardPlugin / SignoffProgressPlugin.
   *
   * This used to POST al_signoff with an @odata.bind to the action (AD-074). No sign-off was
   * ever recorded that way: Power Pages refused the association before any plug-in ran, as
   * it refused the answer create (AD-053) and the claim (AD-076), and the page read the 403
   * as a missing role. So the page now writes one JSON column on the signed-in user's own
   * contact row - the Self-scoped contact permission makes that the only row it can reach -
   * and SignoffRequestPlugin creates the al_signoff server-side after checking the contact
   * holds the T&C Supervisor web role (AD-099). Everything identifying is still stamped by
   * SignoffGuardPlugin; nothing here is a security boundary (NFR-SEC-01).
   */
  (function () {
    'use strict';

    var panels = document.querySelectorAll('[data-ot-signoff]');
    if (!panels.length) { return; }

    var REJECTED = '120910721';
    var contactId = '{{ user.id }}';

    /*
     * The server's own words, out of the response body.
     *
     * The body is an OData error object, so the message has to be read out of it rather than
     * scanned for in the raw text: a prefix found by indexOf and taken to the end of the
     * string carries the JSON tail with it, which is why the branches below used to cut at
     * the next quote and why one of them did not and showed it.
     *
     * A body that will not parse is returned as it stands - it is still more than "something
     * went wrong" - and it is collapsed onto one line and capped, because an error line is
     * read on screen and the whole of a platform fault is not readable there.
     */
    function serverMessage(raw) {
      var text = String(raw || '').trim();
      if (!text) { return ''; }

      var message = text;
      try {
        var body = JSON.parse(text);
        var error = body && body.error ? body.error : body;
        if (error && error.innererror && error.innererror.message) {
          message = error.innererror.message;
        } else if (error && error.message) {
          message = error.message;
        }
      } catch (ignored) {
        // Not JSON. Keep the raw text.
      }

      message = String(message || '').replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim();
      if (message.length > 300) { message = message.substring(0, 300) + '...'; }
      return message;
    }

    function friendlyError(raw, httpStatus) {
      var text = serverMessage(raw);
      if (text.indexOf('PRECONDITION:') !== -1) {
        var idx = text.indexOf('PRECONDITION:');
        return text.substring(idx + 'PRECONDITION:'.length).trim();
      }
      if (text.indexOf('VALIDATION:') !== -1) {
        var v = text.indexOf('VALIDATION:');
        return text.substring(v + 'VALIDATION:'.length).trim();
      }
      if (text.indexOf('UNEXPECTED:') !== -1) {
        var unexpected = text.indexOf('UNEXPECTED:');
        return 'Nothing was recorded. ' + text.substring(unexpected + 'UNEXPECTED:'.length).trim();
      }
      /*
       * Nothing our code raised, so the platform refused before SignoffRequestPlugin ran.
       * Say what the platform said rather than guessing at a role: a 400 is never a
       * permission problem, an association code names the missing grant, and a 403 on this
       * write is the contact permission, which is bound to the reviewer and supervisor
       * roles - the role check itself now answers with a PRECONDITION above.
       */
      if (httpStatus === 400) {
        return 'The portal rejected the request before checking any permission, so nothing was '
          + 'recorded. This is a fault in the page rather than in your account - please report it.';
      }
      var code = /9004010[0-9]/.exec(text);
      if (code) {
        return 'The site refused this write (error ' + code[0] + '), so nothing was recorded. '
          + 'Your role is not the problem - please report it.';
      }
      if (httpStatus === 403) {
        return 'Your portal account is not allowed to write a sign-off request, so nothing was recorded. '
          + 'The contact permission is bound to the reviewer and T&C Supervisor roles; ask an administrator '
          + 'to check your account rather than retrying.';
      }
      if (httpStatus === 401) {
        return 'Your session was not accepted, so nothing was recorded. Reload the page and sign in again.';
      }
      return 'That sign-off was not recorded, and nothing has been changed. '
        + (text ? 'The server said: ' + text : 'The server gave no detail.')
        + (httpStatus ? ' (status ' + httpStatus + ')' : '');
    }

    function wire(panel) {
      // Every action still awaiting a supervisor. One decision covers the remediation
      // (project owner, 2026-09-10), so the same decision and notes are recorded against
      // each of them in turn - the sign-off row is per action because that is what BR-008
      // attests to, but the person makes the judgement once.
      var actionIds = (panel.getAttribute('data-action-ids') || '').split(',');
      var decision = panel.querySelector('[data-ot-signoff-decision]');
      var notes = panel.querySelector('[data-ot-signoff-notes]');
      var grade = panel.querySelector('[data-ot-signoff-outcome]');
      var save = panel.querySelector('[data-ot-signoff-save]');
      var status = panel.querySelector('[data-ot-signoff-status]');

      function show(message, kind) {
        status.textContent = message;
        status.className = 'ot-response__status ot-response__status--' + (kind || 'info');
        status.setAttribute('role', kind === 'error' ? 'alert' : 'status');
      }

      // The words on the option the supervisor chose, for the message and for the cells.
      function decisionLabel() {
        var chosen = decision.options[decision.selectedIndex];
        return chosen ? chosen.textContent.replace(/^\s+|\s+$/g, '') : 'Decision';
      }

      /*
       * What an approval leaves to do, without promising where the case went.
       *
       * The obvious sentences - "the case moves to Awaiting Recheck", "the final outcome is
       * recorded with it, which closes the case" - are both wrong on a Tax leg that still
       * owes an AQS check: approving there returns the case to the QUEUE (OD-038), and no
       * final outcome is recorded because the case never reaches its recheck. The page does
       * not hold the route rules, so it says what is true either way and leaves the state to
       * the badge, which is marked as possibly moved.
       */
      function gradeNote() {
        if (grade && grade.value) {
          return ' The final outcome you chose is recorded with it once the case reaches its'
            + ' recheck, which closes the case.';
        }
        return ' The final outcome is recorded separately, on this page, once the case reaches'
          + ' its recheck.';
      }

      // A decision made is not made again from here; the guard refuses a second one on an
      // action already approved, so the controls go with it.
      function settle() {
        decision.disabled = true;
        notes.disabled = true;
        if (grade) { grade.disabled = true; }
        save.disabled = true;
      }

      save.addEventListener('click', function () {
        if (save.disabled) { return; }

        if (!decision.value) {
          show('Choose whether this remediation is approved or rejected.', 'error');
          return;
        }

        // Told before the round trip; SignoffGuardPlugin refuses it regardless.
        if (decision.value === REJECTED && !notes.value.trim()) {
          show('A rejection must say what the adviser needs to put right.', 'error');
          return;
        }

        // A rejection sends the work back, so it grades nothing. The guard refuses the
        // combination rather than ignoring it, so catch it here where it can be corrected.
        if (decision.value === REJECTED && grade && grade.value) {
          show('A rejection sends the remediation back to the adviser, so it cannot record a final outcome.', 'error');
          return;
        }

        // AD-031: setting a grade records why. Required in SignoffGuardPlugin too, because a
        // page is not a boundary.
        if (grade && grade.value && !notes.value.trim()) {
          show('Recording a final outcome must say why the grade was set.', 'error');
          return;
        }

        if (!window.shell || typeof window.shell.getTokenDeferred !== 'function') {
          show('This page did not load completely. Refresh and try again.', 'error');
          return;
        }

        save.disabled = true;
        show('Recording...', 'info');

        window.shell.getTokenDeferred().done(function (token) {
          var index = 0;

          // One at a time, and a refusal stops the rest: each is a separate write, so
          // firing them together would leave the supervisor guessing which ones landed.
          function next() {
            if (index >= actionIds.length) {
              /*
               * Confirmed in place, for the reason the adviser's form gives above: the rows
               * this wrote are al_signoff and al_remediationaction, the page wrote neither,
               * and a reload inside the change-tracking window re-draws the remediation
               * exactly as it was. Reported on case 254398988 on 2026-09-13, whose six
               * actions were Completed and approved in Dataverse while the page still
               * showed them awaiting a decision.
               */
              settle();
              if (window.otRemediationRows) {
                window.otRemediationRows.decided(
                  actionIds, decisionLabel(), decision.value === REJECTED);
                window.otRemediationRows.supervisorDecided(
                  decisionLabel(), panel.getAttribute('data-user-name') || '',
                  decision.value === REJECTED);
                window.otRemediationRows.caseStatusMayHaveMoved();
              }
              show(decisionLabel() + ', recorded against ' + actionIds.length
                + ' remedial action' + (actionIds.length === 1 ? '' : 's') + '.'
                + (decision.value === REJECTED
                    ? ' The actions go back to the adviser to put right.'
                    : gradeNote())
                + ' Reload the page when you want the rest of it re-read, and if it still'
                + ' shows the old state the site cache has not caught up - try again in a'
                + ' moment.', 'success');
              if (window.otRemediationRows) {
                window.otRemediationRows.offerReload(status);
              }
              return;
            }

            var actionId = actionIds[index];
            if (!actionId) { index += 1; next(); return; }

            // One JSON column on the signatory's own contact row. SignoffRequestPlugin
            // parses it and creates the al_signoff; the browser no longer names a
            // navigation property at all, which is what Power Pages kept refusing.
            var payload = {
              al_signoffrequest: JSON.stringify({
                actionId: actionId,
                decision: Number(decision.value),
                notes: notes.value,
                // Zero where the supervisor left it for a separate regrade, or where the
                // case has no graded outcome and the field was not rendered at all.
                finalOutcome: grade && grade.value ? Number(grade.value) : 0
              })
            };

            var request = new XMLHttpRequest();
            request.open('PATCH', '/_api/contacts(' + contactId + ')', true);
            request.setRequestHeader('Content-Type', 'application/json');
            request.setRequestHeader('__RequestVerificationToken', token);

            request.onreadystatechange = function () {
              if (request.readyState !== 4) { return; }

              if (request.status >= 200 && request.status < 300) {
                index += 1;
                next();
                return;
              }

              show(friendlyError(request.responseText, request.status), 'error');
              save.disabled = false;
            };

            request.send(JSON.stringify(payload));
          }

          next();
        }).fail(function () {
          show('This page did not load completely. Refresh and try again.', 'error');
          save.disabled = false;
        });
      });
    }

    for (var i = 0; i < panels.length; i += 1) {
      wire(panels[i]);
    }
  })();
</script>

<script>
  /*
   * The regrade (OD-041, AD-031, BR-005, BR-007).
   *
   *   page -> PATCH contact.al_regraderequest (JSON)
   *        -> RegradeRequestPlugin  (checks the T&C Supervisor web role)
   *        -> RegradeCasePlugin.Regrade  (the same rules al_RegradeCase enforces)
   *
   * The fourth browser-driven write on this site, and it takes the shape the first three
   * settled on: a Custom API cannot be invoked from a Power Pages page, so the page writes
   * one JSON column on the signed-in user's own contact row - the Self-scoped contact
   * permission makes that the only row it can reach - and the work happens server-side as
   * the application user. Nothing here is a security boundary (NFR-SEC-01): the role is
   * checked in the plug-in, against the contact that was actually written.
   */
  (function () {
    'use strict';

    var panels = document.querySelectorAll('[data-ot-regrade]');
    if (!panels.length) { return; }

    var contactId = '{{ user.id }}';

    // The server's own words, out of the OData error body. Same reasoning as the sign-off's
    // reader above: scanning the raw text for a prefix drags the JSON tail along with it.
    function serverMessage(raw) {
      var text = String(raw || '').trim();
      if (!text) { return ''; }

      var message = text;
      try {
        var body = JSON.parse(text);
        var error = body && body.error ? body.error : body;
        if (error && error.innererror && error.innererror.message) {
          message = error.innererror.message;
        } else if (error && error.message) {
          message = error.message;
        }
      } catch (ignored) {
        // Not JSON. Keep the raw text.
      }

      message = String(message || '').replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim();
      if (message.length > 300) { message = message.substring(0, 300) + '...'; }
      return message;
    }

    function friendlyError(raw, httpStatus) {
      var text = serverMessage(raw);

      var prefixes = ['PRECONDITION:', 'VALIDATION:', 'CONFLICT:'];
      for (var i = 0; i < prefixes.length; i += 1) {
        var at = text.indexOf(prefixes[i]);
        if (at !== -1) {
          return text.substring(at + prefixes[i].length).trim();
        }
      }

      var unexpected = text.indexOf('UNEXPECTED:');
      if (unexpected !== -1) {
        return 'Nothing was recorded. ' + text.substring(unexpected + 'UNEXPECTED:'.length).trim();
      }

      if (httpStatus === 400) {
        return 'The portal rejected the request before checking any permission, so nothing was '
          + 'recorded. This is a fault in the page rather than in your account - please report it.';
      }
      var code = /9004010[0-9]/.exec(text);
      if (code) {
        return 'The site refused this write (error ' + code[0] + '), so nothing was recorded. '
          + 'Your role is not the problem - please report it.';
      }
      if (httpStatus === 403) {
        return 'Your portal account is not allowed to write a regrade request, so nothing was recorded. '
          + 'Ask an administrator to check your account rather than retrying.';
      }
      if (httpStatus === 401) {
        return 'Your session was not accepted, so nothing was recorded. Reload the page and sign in again.';
      }
      return 'That outcome was not recorded, and nothing has been changed. '
        + (text ? 'The server said: ' + text : 'The server gave no detail.')
        + (httpStatus ? ' (status ' + httpStatus + ')' : '');
    }

    function wire(panel) {
      var outcomeId = panel.getAttribute('data-outcome-id') || '';
      var rowVersion = panel.getAttribute('data-row-version') || '';
      var grade = panel.querySelector('[data-ot-regrade-outcome]');
      var reason = panel.querySelector('[data-ot-regrade-reason]');
      var save = panel.querySelector('[data-ot-regrade-save]');
      var status = panel.querySelector('[data-ot-regrade-status]');
      var hint = panel.querySelector('[data-ot-regrade-hint]');

      function show(message, kind) {
        status.textContent = message;
        status.className = 'ot-response__status ot-response__status--' + (kind || 'info');
        status.setAttribute('role', kind === 'error' ? 'alert' : 'status');
      }

      // The panel's own summary line, brought up to date with what was just recorded so
      // the page in hand agrees with Dataverse without waiting for the cache.
      function recorded(label) {
        grade.disabled = true;
        reason.disabled = true;
        save.disabled = true;
        if (!hint) { return; }
        var initial = hint.querySelector('strong');
        var initialText = initial ? initial.textContent : 'not recorded';
        hint.textContent = '';
        hint.appendChild(document.createTextNode('The initial outcome was '));
        var initialNode = document.createElement('strong');
        initialNode.textContent = initialText;
        hint.appendChild(initialNode);
        hint.appendChild(document.createTextNode(', regraded to '));
        var finalNode = document.createElement('strong');
        finalNode.textContent = label;
        hint.appendChild(finalNode);
        hint.appendChild(document.createTextNode(' just now. Recording a final outcome does not change it — both are kept (BR-007).'));
      }

      save.addEventListener('click', function () {
        if (save.disabled) { return; }

        if (!grade.value) {
          show('Choose the final outcome for this case.', 'error');
          return;
        }

        // AD-031 makes this mandatory and RegradeRequestPlugin refuses without it. Told
        // here so the supervisor is not made to wait for a round trip to find out.
        if (!reason.value.trim()) {
          show('A regrade must say why the outcome was changed.', 'error');
          return;
        }

        if (!window.shell || typeof window.shell.getTokenDeferred !== 'function') {
          show('This page did not load completely. Refresh and try again.', 'error');
          return;
        }

        save.disabled = true;
        show('Recording...', 'info');

        window.shell.getTokenDeferred().done(function (token) {
          var payload = {
            al_regraderequest: JSON.stringify({
              outcomeId: outcomeId,
              finalOutcome: grade.value,
              reason: reason.value,
              expectedRowVersion: rowVersion
            })
          };

          var request = new XMLHttpRequest();
          request.open('PATCH', '/_api/contacts(' + contactId + ')', true);
          request.setRequestHeader('Content-Type', 'application/json');
          request.setRequestHeader('__RequestVerificationToken', token);

          request.onreadystatechange = function () {
            if (request.readyState !== 4) { return; }

            if (request.status >= 200 && request.status < 300) {
              // Confirmed in place, and no reload. The rows a regrade writes are the
              // outcome and the case, and this page did not write them - it wrote the
              // request column and RegradeRequestPlugin did the rest - so the portal's
              // render cache is not cleared by this write and learns through change
              // tracking, which is polled (AD-094, AD-117). A reload inside that window
              // re-drew the old grade under a success message, and was read as "it did
              // not save" on IO-300005 and again on case 254398988. The controls stay
              // disabled: the row version this panel holds is now stale, and a further
              // regrade has to start from a fresh read.
              recorded(grade.value);
              if (window.otRemediationRows) {
                window.otRemediationRows.regraded(grade.value);
              }
              show('Final outcome recorded as ' + grade.value + ', with your reason written to the audit history of the case.'
                + ' The Regraded outcome and the case status above now show it, and the case is closed.'
                + ' Reload the page when you want the rest of it re-read, and if it still shows the old state the site'
                + ' cache has not caught up - try again in a moment.', 'success');
              if (window.otRemediationRows) {
                window.otRemediationRows.offerReload(status);
              }
              return;
            }

            show(friendlyError(request.responseText, request.status), 'error');
            save.disabled = false;
          };

          request.send(JSON.stringify(payload));
        }).fail(function () {
          show('This page did not load completely. Refresh and try again.', 'error');
          save.disabled = false;
        });
      });
    }

    for (var i = 0; i < panels.length; i += 1) {
      wire(panels[i]);
    }
  })();
</script>
{% endblock %}
"
}
